WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:05.020
Well before the Marvel Cinematic Universe
ruled the world, indie writer/director Kevin

00:00:05.020 --> 00:00:07.880
Smith was ahead of the game with his own "View
Askewniverse."

00:00:07.880 --> 00:00:11.780
Now, the filmmaker is ready to take us back
there with Jay and Silent Bob Reboot.

00:00:11.780 --> 00:00:16.300
If you're wondering what it's all about, we've
got the answers to all your blunt questions.

00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:21.380
In keeping with Kevin Smith's indie film roots,
Jay and Silent Bob Reboot will roll out in

00:00:21.380 --> 00:00:24.020
a slightly different manner than most major
movies do.

00:00:24.020 --> 00:00:28.740
Fathom Events, which distributes special and
live events to select multiplexes, will handle

00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:32.180
Reboot's first showings on October 15, 2019.

00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:36.820
These special screenings will include an introduction
from Smith, some bonus material, and free

00:00:36.820 --> 00:00:38.840
movie posters for lucky fans.

00:00:38.840 --> 00:00:42.980
Two days later, Reboot will screen again as
part of a double feature alongside Jay and

00:00:42.980 --> 00:00:44.420
Silent Bob Strike Back.

00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:47.680
"Jay and Silent Bob only work in small doses,
if at all.

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:48.780
They don't deserve their own movie."

00:00:49.180 --> 00:00:50.180
"He's got a point-"

00:00:50.180 --> 00:00:51.160
"F--- him.

00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:51.860
What's the next one say?"

00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:56.100
After those initial events, Smith and Mewes
are taking the show on the road.

00:00:56.100 --> 00:01:00.460
The pair will travel around the U.S. to personally
present the film and follow it up with Q&amp;A

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:01.260
sessions.

00:01:01.260 --> 00:01:06.860
Between October 21 and December 12, "The Jay
&amp; Silent Bob Reboot Roadshow" will hit 31

00:01:06.860 --> 00:01:08.660
cities for 45 screenings.

00:01:08.840 --> 00:01:11.800
"So come on out and join us and give us your
money because we gotta eat this year."

00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:16.480
Kevin Smith has been doing his own thing in
the movie industry for 25 years.

00:01:16.480 --> 00:01:21.240
In that time, he's built up a massive world
of characters within his View Askewniverse,

00:01:21.240 --> 00:01:24.320
and Jay and Silent Bob Reboot is bringing
back a ton of them.

00:01:24.320 --> 00:01:29.380
Jason Mewes and Kevin Smith are back as the
titular duo, while Jason Lee once again plays

00:01:29.380 --> 00:01:32.700
Brodie Bruce, his comics-loving character
from Mallrats.

00:01:32.700 --> 00:01:37.900
Joey Lauren Adams will appear as her Chasing
Amy comics creator Alyssa Jones, as will Ben

00:01:37.909 --> 00:01:41.440
Affleck, returning as his Chasing Amy character
Holden McNeil.

00:01:41.440 --> 00:01:45.770
Affleck's frequent collaborator Matt Damon
will also make an appearance, likely portraying

00:01:45.770 --> 00:01:49.440
Loki, his Dogma character, though he's also
appeared in the franchise playing a version

00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:50.500
of himself.

00:01:51.240 --> 00:01:53.640
"It's hunting season."

00:01:53.840 --> 00:01:59.060
Rosario Dawson has signed on to play Becky,
the role she originated in Clerks II, alongside

00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:02.220
Brian O'Halloran, returning as Clerks protagonist
Dante.

00:02:02.540 --> 00:02:04.740
"I'm not even supposed to be here today!"

00:02:04.880 --> 00:02:10.240
It's not all Kevin Smith veterans along for
the ride, though; Val Kilmer, Melissa Benoist,

00:02:10.250 --> 00:02:14.780
Joe Manganiello, Justin Long, Craig Robinson,
and Chris Hemsworth are also set to make the

00:02:14.780 --> 00:02:17.320
leap into the Askewniverse for the first time.

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:23.220
Yes, Jay and Silent Bob Reboot will revisit
the world of Smith's classic '90s comedies,

00:02:23.220 --> 00:02:24.440
just as fans remember them.

00:02:24.440 --> 00:02:29.580
It's a self-aware movie, making fun of both
itself and Hollywood's obsession with retreads.

00:02:29.580 --> 00:02:35.540
According to Smith, speaking at a post-podcast-taping
Q&amp;A in May 2019, the movie follows what happens

00:02:35.540 --> 00:02:36.360
when,

00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:40.420
"Jay and Silent Bob find out that Hollywood
is making a reboot of that old movie that

00:02:40.420 --> 00:02:44.650
they had made about them [in Jay and Silent
Bob Strike Back], and they have to go cross

00:02:44.650 --> 00:02:47.440
the country to Hollywood to stop it all over
again."

00:02:47.440 --> 00:02:51.620
Smith is well aware of the irony of the situation,
adding the observation,

00:02:51.620 --> 00:02:55.790
"It's a movie that makes fun of sequels and
remakes and reboots while being all three

00:02:55.790 --> 00:02:56.980
at the same time."

00:02:56.980 --> 00:03:01.260
Along with the road trip to stop a movie from
getting made (again), there's a major plot

00:03:01.270 --> 00:03:05.150
addition: Jay has a child, a young woman named
Millennium Faulken.

00:03:05.150 --> 00:03:09.630
"Millie" is a lot like her father in that
she also has a constant companion who never

00:03:09.630 --> 00:03:11.720
speaks, a deaf friend named Soapy.

00:03:11.720 --> 00:03:13.880
They insist on heading to Hollywood, too.

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:19.920
On July 18, 2019, movie distributor Saban
Films released the first trailer for Jay and

00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:21.240
Silent Bob Reboot.

00:03:21.240 --> 00:03:26.140
The profanity-laden preview proves that Reboot
does indeed imitate the plot of Jay and Silent

00:03:26.140 --> 00:03:29.920
Bob Strike Back, while also making fun of
that movie, and Hollywood, too.

00:03:29.920 --> 00:03:34.320
Jay and Silent Bob Strike Back concerns the
duo's trip to Hollywood to shutter a movie

00:03:34.320 --> 00:03:39.820
version of Bluntman and Chronic, a marijuana-meets-Batman
style comic book created by Ben Affleck's

00:03:39.820 --> 00:03:41.360
character Holden McNeil.

00:03:41.360 --> 00:03:46.040
Jason Biggs and James Van Der Beek appear
as themselves as the stars of the adaptation.

00:03:46.040 --> 00:03:50.280
Along the way, Jay meets and falls for an
animal rights activist named Justice, played

00:03:50.290 --> 00:03:51.680
by Shannon Elizabeth.

00:03:51.680 --> 00:03:55.940
According to the Jay and Silent Bob Reboot
trailer, the new movie centers on a reboot

00:03:55.940 --> 00:04:00.290
of the Bluntman and Chronic movie in production,
with Val Kilmer and Melissa Benoist taking

00:04:00.290 --> 00:04:02.960
on the roles in a winking nod to their other
jobs.

00:04:02.960 --> 00:04:05.520
Biggs and Van Der Beek do return for a cameo,
though.

00:04:05.720 --> 00:04:07.260
"Who's directing this s--- anyway?

00:04:07.260 --> 00:04:09.000
Kevin f---ing Smith?"

00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:13.740
Along the way, Jay reconnects with Justice,
who introduces him to their teenage daughter,

00:04:13.740 --> 00:04:16.740
played by Harley Quinn Smith, Smith's real-life
daughter.

00:04:16.740 --> 00:04:21.080
Jay and Silent Bob diehards can also get a
load of the official Jay and Silent Bob Reboot

00:04:21.080 --> 00:04:21.760
poster.

00:04:21.760 --> 00:04:26.120
This winking-at-the-past key art is consistent
with the rest of the movie in its nod to the

00:04:26.121 --> 00:04:30.979
past, as the poster depicts Jason Mewes and
Kevin Smith in character standing against

00:04:30.980 --> 00:04:35.300
a brick wall, not unlike the one they leaned
against in Clerks back in 1994.

00:04:35.300 --> 00:04:39.820
Smith also unveiled a movie poster for the
movie-within-a-movie, advertising the Bluntman

00:04:39.820 --> 00:04:41.160
and Chronic reboot.

00:04:41.160 --> 00:04:46.260
It strikes a dark, gritty tone, reminiscent
of the DC Comics movie starring one of the

00:04:46.260 --> 00:04:49.900
View Askewniverse's most successful alumni:
Ben Affleck.

00:04:50.160 --> 00:04:52.620
"Affleck was the bomb in Phantoms."

00:04:52.620 --> 00:04:53.560
"Word, b----.

00:04:53.560 --> 00:04:55.620
Phantoms like a motherf-----."

